Here is a description of the Terraform program that will define a valid Route 53 zone association resource:

**Description:**
This Terraform configuration will create a new Route 53 hosted zone and associate it with an existing AWS account's hosted zone. This association will enable DNS queries for the hosted zone to be routed to the AWS account's DNS service.

**Terraform HCL Program:**
```hcl
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
  default_tags {
    tags = {
      Environment = "dev"
    }
  }
}

# Create a new Route 53 hosted zone
resource "aws_route53_zone" "example" {
  name = "example.com"
}

# Create a new Route 53 zone association
resource "aws_route53_zone_association" "example" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example.id
}
```
This configuration assumes that you have the AWS provider configured and authenticated with your AWS account. The `aws_route53_zone` resource creates a new hosted zone with the name "example.com", and the `aws_route53_zone_association` resource associates this zone with the existing hosted zone in your AWS account.

