This configuration creates:

* An IAM instance profile called `eb_ec2_profile`
* An IAM role called `eb_ec2_role` with an attached policy that grants read-only access to EC2
* An Elastic Beanstalk environment called `my-env` with a web server tier and a version label of `v1`
* A MySQL RDS instance called `default` with a default password and username
* A security group called `db-sg` that allows incoming traffic on port 3306 from any IP address.

Note: You should replace the `my-keypair`, `myuser`, `mypassword`, and `vpc-12345678` placeholders with your actual values.

