Here is a description of the Terraform program I will define:

**Program Description**

This Terraform program will create an AWS CodeBuild project with an example IAM role and secondary sources. The program will define the following resources:

* An IAM role with a policy that grants CodeBuild permission to access the AWS CodePipeline service.
* An IAM role policy that grants CodeBuild permission to read from the AWS CodeCommit repository.
* A secondary source in the CodeBuild project that points to the AWS CodeCommit repository.
* A CodeBuild project resource that uses the example IAM role.

**Terraform HCL Program**
```terraform
# Configure the AWS provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an IAM role with a policy that grants CodeBuild permission to access the AWS CodePipeline service
resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild-role" {
  name        = "codebuild-role"
  description = "IAM role for CodeBuild"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create an IAM role policy that grants CodeBuild permission to read from the AWS CodeCommit repository
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "codebuild-codecommit-policy" {
  name   = "codebuild-codecommit-policy"
  role   = aws_iam_role.codebuild-role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "codecommit:GetCommit",
          "codecommit:GetFile",
          "codecommit:GetFileContent"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = aws_codecommit_repository.codecommit-repo.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create a secondary source in the CodeBuild project that points to the AWS CodeCommit repository
resource "aws_codebuild_project_source" "codecommit-source" {
  project_name = aws_codebuild_project.codebuild-project.name
  source_type  = "CODECOMMIT"

  source_location = aws_codecommit_repository.codecommit-repo.clone_url
  source_version  = "master"
}

# Create a CodeBuild project resource that uses the example IAM role
resource "aws_codebuild_project" "codebuild-project" {
  name = "example-codebuild-project"

  source {
    type     = "CODECOMMIT"
    location = aws_codecommit_repository.codecommit-repo.clone_url
    version  = "master"
  }

  environment {
    compute_type                = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
    image                       = "aws/codebuild/nodejs:10.0"
    type                        = "LINUX_CONTAINER"
  }

  service_role = aws_iam_role.codebuild-role.arn

  artifacts {
    type = "CODEPIPELINE"
  }
}
```
Note that I used the `aws_codecommit_repository` resource to create a CodeCommit repository, which is not shown in this example. You will need to add this resource to your Terraform configuration if you want to create a new CodeCommit repository.

