**Terraform Program Description**

The Terraform program will create an AWS Lex bot with multiple slots. The bot will be created in the US East (N. Virginia) region. The program will define the following resources:

* An IAM role to allow Lex to access other AWS services
* An AWS Lex bot with multiple slots, including a slot for user's name, age, and phone number
* A slot type for each of the above slots
* An intent with a sample utterance and a response message

**Terraform HCL Program**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

# Create an IAM role for Lex to access other AWS services
resource "aws_iam_role" "lex_role" {
  name        = "lex-role"
  description = "Role for Lex to access other AWS services"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lex.us-east-1.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach the necessary policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_policy" "lex_policy" {
  name        = "lex-policy"
  description = "Policy for Lex to access other AWS services"

  policy      = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "logs:CreateLogGroup"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "logs:CreateLogStream"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "logs:PutLogEvents"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "lex_attach" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.lex_role.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.lex_policy.arn
}

# Create a slot type for user's name
resource "aws_lex_slot_type" "name_slot" {
  name       = "name-slot"
  description = "Slot for user's name"

  enumeration_values = [
    {
      value = "John"
    },
    {
      value = "Jane"
    }
  ]
}

# Create a slot type for user's age
resource "aws_lex_slot_type" "age_slot" {
  name       = "age-slot"
  description = "Slot for user's age"

  enumeration_values = [
    {
      value = "18"
    },
    {
      value = "19"
    }
  ]
}

# Create a slot type for user's phone number
resource "aws_lex_slot_type" "phone_slot" {
  name       = "phone-slot"
  description = "Slot for user's phone number"

  enumeration_values = [
    {
      value = "+1234567890"
    },
    {
      value = "+9876543210"
    }
  ]
}

# Create an intent with a sample utterance and a response message
resource "aws_lex_intent" "greeting_intent" {
  name        = "greeting-intent"
  description = "Intent to greet the user"

  sample_utterances = [
    {
      text = "hello"
    }
  ]

  response_messages = [
    {
      text = "Hi! How can I help you today?"
    }
  ]
}

# Create the bot
resource "aws_lex_bot" "example_bot" {
  name        = "example-bot"
  description = "Bot to demonstrate multiple slots"

  intents = [
    aws_lex_intent.greeting_intent.id
  ]

  slots = [
    aws_lex_slot_type.name_slot.id,
    aws_lex_slot_type.age_slot.id,
    aws_lex_slot_type.phone_slot.id
  ]
}
```

This Terraform program defines the necessary resources to create an AWS Lex bot with multiple slots. The bot will have three slots: "name-slot", "age-slot", and "phone-slot", and one intent "greeting-intent". The program uses the `aws_iam_role` and `aws_iam_policy` resources to create an IAM role for Lex to access other AWS services. The `aws_lex_slot_type` and `aws_lex_intent` resources are used to create the slot types and intent for the bot. The `aws_lex_bot` resource is used to create the bot itself, attaching the intents and slots to the bot.

