**AWS IAM Role Policy for EKS**
```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "example" {
  name   = "example-eks-cluster-policy"
  role   = aws_iam_role.example.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "ec2:DescribeSubnets",
          "ec2:DescribeSecurityGroups",
          "ec2:DescribeVpcs",
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "eks:UpdateClusterConfig"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = aws_eks_cluster.example.arn
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

**EKS Addon Resource**
```hcl
resource "aws_eks_addon" "example" {
  cluster_name = aws_eks_cluster.example.name
  addon_name   = "vpc-cni"
  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy.example]
}
```

**Subnets (Required for EKS Cluster)**
```hcl
resource "aws_subnet" "example" {
  count             = 2
  cidr_block        = cidrsubnet("10.0.0.0/16", 8, count.index)
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.example.id
  availability_zone = var.region == "us-west-2" ? "us-west-2a" : "us-west-2b"
  map_public_ip_on_launch = true
}
```

**VPC (Required for EKS Cluster)**
```hcl
resource "aws_vpc" "example" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}
```

This Terraform script will create an AWS EKS cluster with a name specified by the `cluster_name` variable, an IAM role and policy for the EKS cluster, and an EKS addon named "vpc-cni". The script also creates a VPC and 2 subnets for the EKS cluster.

