**Terraform Configuration: AWS EKS Cluster and IAM Role**

The following Terraform configuration will create an AWS IAM role (demo_eks) for an Amazon EKS cluster and an EKS cluster itself with specified VPC configurations.

**Note:** Make sure to replace the `aws_region` variable with your preferred AWS region.

```hcl
# File: main.tf

# Provider Configuration
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# IAM Role for EKS Cluster
resource "aws_iam_role" "demo_eks" {
  name        = "demo_eks"
  description = "EKS Cluster Role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach IAM Policies to EKS Role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "demo_eks" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.demo_eks.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "demo_eks_vpc" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.demo_eks.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSVPCResourceController"
}

# EKS Cluster Configuration
resource "aws_eks_cluster" "demo_eks" {
  name     = "demo-eks"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.demo_eks.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = [
      "subnet-12345678",
      "subnet-90123456"
    ]
  }

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.demo_eks,
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.demo_eks_vpc,
  ]
}

# Output the EKS Cluster endpoint
output "endpoint" {
  value = aws_eks_cluster.demo_eks.endpoint
}
```

This configuration creates an IAM role (`demo_eks`) with the necessary permissions to manage an EKS cluster, attaches the required policies, and then creates the EKS cluster itself with the specified VPC configurations. The `depends_on` meta-attribute is used to ensure that the EKS cluster is created after the IAM policies are attached.

Make sure to replace the `aws_region` variable with your preferred AWS region and update the `subnet-ids` to match your actual VPC subnets.

