**Description of the Terraform Program**

This Terraform program will create an AWS S3 bucket named 'example-bucket' with object lock enabled. Object lock will be configured with a governance mode and a retention period of 90 days for all objects stored in the bucket.

**Terraform HCL Program**
```terraform
# Configure the AWS provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define the S3 bucket resource
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example_bucket" {
  bucket = "example-bucket"
  acl    = "private"

  # Enable object lock
  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }

  # Configure object lock
  object_lock_configuration {
    enabled = true
    rule {
      defaultRetention {
        mode = "GOVERNANCE"
        days = 90
      }
    }
  }
}

# Define the S3 bucket policy (required for object lock)
resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "example_bucket_policy" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid       = "AllowRootAccess"
        Effect    = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "s3.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action     = "s3:PutObject"
        Resource  = "${aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.arn}/*"
      },
      {
        Sid       = "DenyRootDelete"
        Effect    = "Deny"
        Principal = {
          Service = "s3.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action     = "s3:DeleteObject"
        Resource  = "${aws_s3_bucket.example_bucket.arn}/*"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```
This Terraform program defines two resources:

1. `aws_s3_bucket`: Creates the S3 bucket named 'example-bucket' with object lock enabled.
2. `aws_s3_bucket_policy`: Defines an S3 bucket policy that is required for object lock to function correctly. The policy allows root access for putting objects in the bucket and denies root access for deleting objects.

Note that this program uses the `aws` provider with a region set to `us-west-2`. You can modify the region as needed.

To apply this configuration, run `terraform init` followed by `terraform apply`.

