**Description of the Terraform Program**

The Terraform program will create an AWS Lambda function called "example_lambda" with a basic execution role. It will then create an AWS Lambda execution role and attach the necessary policies to allow the Lambda function to be invoked. Finally, it will invoke the Lambda function using the `aws_lambda_invoke` resource.

**Terraform HCL Program**

```terraform
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an AWS Lambda execution role
resource "aws_iam_role" "lambda_exec_role" {
  name        = "example_lambda_exec_role"
  description = "Execution role for the example Lambda function"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lambda.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create an AWS Lambda policy to allow execution
resource "aws_iam_policy" "lambda_exec_policy" {
  name        = "example_lambda_exec_policy"
  description = "Policy for executing the example Lambda function"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "logs:CreateLogGroup"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "logs:CreateLogStream"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Action = "logs:PutLogEvents"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach the Lambda execution policy to the execution role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "lambda_exec_attach" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.lambda_exec_role.name
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.lambda_exec_policy.arn
}

# Create an AWS Lambda function
resource "aws_lambda_function" "example_lambda" {
  filename      = "lambda_function_payload.zip"
  function_name = "example_lambda"
  handler       = "index.handler"
  runtime       = "nodejs14.x"
  role          = aws_iam_role.lambda_exec_role.arn

  # Note: In a real-world scenario, you would upload the zip file to the AWS Lambda console or use the `aws_lambda_function` resource's `file` argument.
  # For this example, we'll assume the zip file is already uploaded to the console.
}

# Invoke the AWS Lambda function
resource "null_resource" "invoke_lambda" {
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = "aws lambda invoke --function-name ${aws_lambda_function.example_lambda.function_name} --payload '{}'"
  }
}
```

This configuration assumes that the Lambda function is implemented in Node.js and is stored in a zip file called `lambda_function_payload.zip`. The function's `handler` is set to `index.handler`, which means the function will look for an `index.handler` function in the zip file. The Lambda function's execution role is attached to the `aws_lambda_exec_role` role, which has the necessary policies to allow the function to execute. Finally, the `null_resource` is used to invoke the Lambda function using the `aws lambda invoke` command.

