**Terraform Program Description:**

This Terraform program will create a managed Amazon MSK (Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka) cluster with encryption at rest. It will define the necessary AWS resources, including:

1. An IAM role for the MSK cluster with the required permissions.
2. An MSK cluster with encryption at rest using a customer-managed key (CMK) from AWS Key Management Service (KMS).
3. The program will deploy the MSK cluster in a specified AWS region and Availability Zone.

**Terraform HCL Program:**
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
  version = "4.25.0"
}

variable "msk_cluster_name" {
  type        = string
  default     = "my-msk-cluster"
}

variable "msk_cluster_encryption_key_arn" {
  type        = string
  default     = "arn:aws:kms:us-west-2:123456789012:key/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"
}

variable "msk_cluster_vpc_id" {
  type        = string
  default     = "vpc-12345678"
}

variable "msk_cluster_subnet_ids" {
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-90123456"]
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "msk_cluster_role" {
  name        = "${var.msk_cluster_name}-msk-cluster-role"
  description = "MSK Cluster IAM Role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kafka.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kms_key" "msk_cluster_key" {
  description             = "MSK Cluster Encryption Key"
  deletion_window_in_days = 10
}

resource "aws_msk_cluster" "msk_cluster" {
  cluster_name        = var.msk_cluster_name
  kafka_version       = "2.6.1"
  number_of_broker_nodes = 3
  broker_node_type    = "kafka.m5.large"
  enhancedMonitoring = true
  encryption_info {
    encryption_at_rest {
      kms_key_arn = aws_kms_key.msk_cluster_key.arn
    }
  }
  vpc_ids     = [var.msk_cluster_vpc_id]
  subnet_ids  = var.msk_cluster_subnet_ids
  iam_role_arn = aws_iam_role.msk_cluster_role.arn
}
```
This Terraform program defines the necessary resources to create a managed MSK cluster with encryption at rest. The program uses the `aws` provider to interact with AWS services. The `aws_iam_role` resource creates the IAM role for the MSK cluster, and the `aws_kms_key` resource creates a customer-managed key (CMK) for encryption at rest. The `aws_msk_cluster` resource creates the MSK cluster with the specified configuration.

