**Terraform Program Description**
================================

This Terraform program will create a DynamoDB table with replicas in two regions: us-east-2 and us-west-2. The program will define the necessary IAM roles and permissions for the DynamoDB table, as well as the DynamoDB table itself with the specified replicas.

**Terraform HCL Program**
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

# Define a DynamoDB table with replicas in us-east-2 and us-west-2
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name         = "example-table"
  billing_mode = "PROVISIONED"
  read_capacity_units = 1
  write_capacity_units = 1

  hash_key       = "id"
  range_key      = "sort_key"

  # Replicas in us-east-2 and us-west-2
  global_secondary_index {
    hash_key         = "id"
    range_key        = "sort_key"
    replication_scope = "REGIONAL"
    non_key_attributes = []
    provisioned_throughput {
      read_capacity_units = 1
      write_capacity_units = 1
    }
    replication_tags {
      region_name = "us-east-2"
    }
  }

  global_secondary_index {
    hash_key         = "id"
    range_key        = "sort_key"
    replication_scope = "REGIONAL"
    non_key_attributes = []
    provisioned_throughput {
      read_capacity_units = 1
      write_capacity_units = 1
    }
    replication_tags {
      region_name = "us-west-2"
    }
  }
}

# Create an IAM role for the DynamoDB table
resource "aws_iam_role" "example_role" {
  name = "example-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dynamodb.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach the IAM role to the DynamoDB table
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  # ...

  iam_role      = aws_iam_role.example_role.arn
  iam_role_name = aws_iam_role.example_role.name
}
```
This Terraform program defines a DynamoDB table with replicas in us-east-2 and us-west-2, as well as the necessary IAM role for the table. The IAM role is created with the necessary permissions for the DynamoDB table. The DynamoDB table is then attached to the IAM role.

