3. An IAM Role for Redshift, which allows the Redshift cluster to execute S3 operations.
4. An IAM Policy for Redshift, which grants S3 read access to the specified bucket.
5. An IAM Role Policy Attachment, which attaches the IAM policy to the Redshift IAM role.
6. A Redshift Event Subscription, which subscribes to events such as cluster join and leave.

Note that you will need to replace the placeholders with your own values (e.g., bucket name, password, etc.).

