Here is the Terraform HCL program that defines a basic AWS IAM group with an example group policy attachment resource attaching a policy to it:

**main.tf**
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define the IAM group
resource "aws_iam_group" "example_group" {
  name = "example_group"
}

# Define the IAM group policy attachment
resource "aws_iam_group_policy_attachment" "example_attach" {
  group      = aws_iam_group.example_group.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
}
```
In this configuration, we define an AWS provider in the `us-west-2` region. We then define an IAM group named `example_group`. Finally, we define an IAM group policy attachment that attaches the `AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess` policy to the `example_group`.

Note that this configuration will create the necessary IAM resources in the specified AWS region. If you run `terraform apply`, Terraform will prompt you to confirm the creation of these resources.

As an added touch, you can declare a variable to make it easier to change the region or policy ARN:
```terraform
variable "aws_region" {
  type        = string
  default     = "us-west-2"
}

variable "policy_arn" {
  type        = string
  default     = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
}
```
This way, you can modify the `aws_region` and `policy_arn` variables as needed. The provider configuration would then be updated to use the values of these variables:
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  region = var.aws_region
}
```
The group policy attachment resource would remain unchanged.

