**Description of the Terraform Program:**
This Terraform program will create an Amazon Lightsail instance with multiple attached disks. The instance will be deployed in the us-west-2 region (Oregon) and will have a single container-based instance type (e.g. "ls-2c-2xlarge"). The program will also create three attached disks with varying sizes (8 GB, 16 GB, and 32 GB) to demonstrate multiple disk attachment.

**Terraform HCL Program:**
```terraform
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define a variable for the instance type and default to a small instance
variable "instance_type" {
  type = string
  default = "ls-2c-2xlarge"
}

# Create an IAM role for the Lightsail instance
resource "aws_iam_role" "lightsail_instance" {
  name = "lightsail-instance-role"
  description = "Lightsail instance role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lightsail.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create a Lightsail instance
resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "example" {
  name = "example-lightsail-instance"
  instance_type = var.instance_type
  iam_instance_profile_name = aws_iam_role.lightsail_instance.name
}

# Create three attached disks with varying sizes
resource "aws_lightsail_disk" "disks" {
  count = 3
  name = "disk-${count.index + 1}"
  size_in_gb = count.index == 0 ? 8 : (count.index == 1 ? 16 : 32)
  instance_name = aws_lightsail_instance.example.name
}

output "instance_ip" {
  value = aws_lightsail_instance.example.ip_address
}
```
This Terraform program creates a Lightsail instance with multiple attached disks. The `aws_iam_role` resource creates an IAM role for the instance, and the `aws_lightsail_instance` resource creates the instance with the specified instance type. The `aws_lightsail_disk` resource creates three attached disks with varying sizes. The `output` block outputs the IP address of the Lightsail instance.

