**Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform program will create an AWS Elastic File System (EFS) with automatic backups enabled. The EFS will be created in the specified region and will be configured to automatically back up its data on a daily basis.

**Terraform HCL Program:**
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_efs_file_system" "example" {
  creation_token = "example-efs"

  tags = {
    Name        = "example-efs"
    Environment = "dev"
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_mount_target" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id
  subnet_id      = "subnet-12345678"

  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.example.id]
}

resource "aws_security_group" "example" {
  name        = "example-efs-sg"
  description = "Security group for example EFS"

  ingress {
    from_port   = 2049
    to_port     = 2049
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_efs_backup_policy" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id

  daily_backup {
    enabled = true
  }
}
```
**Explanation:**

* We define the AWS provider with the `region` set to `us-west-2`.
* We create an AWS EFS resource with a `creation_token` and `tags` to identify it.
* We create an AWS EFS Mount Target resource to associate the EFS with a subnet and security group.
* We create an AWS Security Group resource to allow inbound traffic on port 2049 (the default port for EFS).
* We create an AWS EFS Backup Policy resource to enable automatic backups of the EFS on a daily basis.

**Note:** Make sure to replace `subnet-12345678` with the actual subnet ID where your EFS will be deployed, and update the security group configuration as needed. Also, ensure that you have the necessary permissions to create EFS and backup policy resources in your AWS account.

