**Terraform Program Description:**
This Terraform configuration will create an AWS EFS file system and a mount target for it. The EFS file system will be created in a specific region, and the mount target will be created in a specified Availability Zone (AZ). The configuration will also define an IAM role with the necessary permissions to access the EFS file system.

**Terraform HCL Program:**
```terraform
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define the EFS file system
resource "aws_efs_file_system" "example" {
  creation_token = "exampleefs"
  performance_mode = "generalPurpose"
  throughput_mode  = "bursting"

  tags = {
    Name = "example-efs"
  }
}

# Define the IAM role for EFS access
resource "aws_iam_role" "efs-role" {
  name        = "efs-role"
  description = "EFS role for example-efs"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach the IAM role policy to the EFS role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "efs-policy" {
  name   = "efs-policy"
  role   = aws_iam_role.efs-role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "elasticfilesystem:*"
        Resource = aws_efs_file_system.example.id
        Effect = "Allow"
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create the EFS mount target
resource "aws_efs_mount_target" "example" {
  file_system_id = aws_efs_file_system.example.id
  subnet_id      = "subnet-12345678"
  security_groups = [aws_security_group.example.id]
}

# Create a security group for the EFS mount target
resource "aws_security_group" "example" {
  name        = "example-sg"
  description = "Security group for example-efs"

  ingress {
    from_port   = 2049
    to_port     = 2049
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}
```
This configuration creates:

1. An AWS EFS file system named "exampleefs"
2. An IAM role with the necessary permissions to access the EFS file system
3. An IAM role policy attached to the IAM role
4. An EFS mount target in a specified subnet and security group
5. A security group for the EFS mount target

Note that you should replace the `subnet-12345678` and `0.0.0.0/0` values with your actual subnet ID and IP range, respectively. Additionally, this configuration assumes that you have the necessary credentials and permissions to create AWS resources.

