**Description of the Terraform Program**

The Terraform program will configure an AWS environment as the cloud provider. It will define a custom AWS VPC with a specific CIDR block of 10.0.0.0/16 and a network ACL linked to this VPC that allows specific TCP traffic for both ingress and egress rules. The program will create IAM roles as needed and provide default values for any variables used. The configuration will be valid and deployable.

**Terraform HCL Program**
```hcl
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define the VPC
resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
  tags = {
    Name = "main-vpc"
  }
}

# Define the Network ACL
resource "aws_network_acl" "main" {
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id
  tags = {
    Name = "main-nacl"
  }

  # Allow inbound traffic on TCP ports 22, 80, and 443
  ingress_rule {
    rule_number = 100
    protocol    = "tcp"
    rule_action = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
    from_port   = 22
    to_port     = 22
  }

  ingress_rule {
    rule_number = 101
    protocol    = "tcp"
    rule_action = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
  }

  ingress_rule {
    rule_number = 102
    protocol    = "tcp"
    rule_action = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
    from_port   = 443
    to_port     = 443
  }

  # Allow outbound traffic on TCP ports 80 and 443
  egress_rule {
    rule_number = 100
    protocol    = "tcp"
    rule_action = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
  }

  egress_rule {
    rule_number = 101
    protocol    = "tcp"
    rule_action = "allow"
    cidr_block  = "0.0.0.0/0"
    from_port   = 443
    to_port     = 443
  }
}
```
This Terraform program will create an AWS VPC with the specified CIDR block and a network ACL that allows inbound traffic on TCP ports 22, 80, and 443, and outbound traffic on TCP ports 80 and 443.
